@startuml Round_State_Machine
skinparam state {
    BorderColor #2C3E50
    BackgroundColor #ECF0F1
    ArrowColor #2980B9
}
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

title Federated Learning - Round State Machine (one round)

[*] --> OPEN : Coordinator opens round t\n(new round_id)
note right of OPEN
  - Global model v_t published to file storage (+ SHA-256)
  - Random subset of available, conformant clients
    selected (configurable fraction, fixed seed)
  - Round deadline written to PostgreSQL
end note

OPEN --> COLLECTING : Tasks published to selected clients\n(clients receive them via GET /task polling)
note right of COLLECTING
  Gateway accepts POST /update:
  - Client token verified
  - SHA-256 checksum verified
  - Same update_id again -> idempotent OK (retry)
  - Other update for same (run, round, client) -> duplicate, rejected
  - Closed round / old model version -> stale, rejected
end note

COLLECTING --> AGGREGATING : All selected clients reported\nOR (deadline reached AND received >= min_participants)
note right of AGGREGATING
  - Updates arriving now are rejected as stale
  - Weighted average of client weights (FedAvg / FedProx)
  - Evaluate v_{t+1} on server-side held-out test set
  - Persist new model + round metrics
end note

COLLECTING --> FAILED : Deadline reached AND received < min_participants
OPEN --> FAILED : Not enough available clients
AGGREGATING --> FAILED : Aggregation / evaluation error
note right of FAILED
  - Failure reason recorded in PostgreSQL
  - Global model stays at v_t
end note

AGGREGATING --> DONE : Global model v_{t+1} saved

DONE --> [*]
FAILED --> [*]

note as RunLevel
  Every state transition is persisted to PostgreSQL before the next step,
  so a restarted coordinator can resume the run.
  Run level (outside this diagram): after DONE or FAILED the coordinator opens
  the next round with a new round_id, until the configured number of rounds is reached;
  then the final model is packaged (safetensors + ONNX + SHA-256) and the report is generated.
end note

@enduml
